.TH AM 1 "November 2025" "2.3.1" "Alias Manager"
.SH NAME
am \- manage shell aliases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY am
.B init
.RI [ shell ]
.YS
.SY am
.B add
.I name
.I command
.YS
.SY am
.B rm
.I name
.RB [ \-f ]
.YS
.SY am
.B ls
.RI [ pattern ]
.YS
.SY am
.B reload
.RI [ shell ]
.YS
.SY am
.B path
.YS
.SY am
.B help | version
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B am
is a lightweight CLI tool for managing shell aliases.
Aliases are stored in a plain text file and can be loaded into any POSIX shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI init " " \fR[\fIshell\fR]
Interactive setup that adds alias loading to your shell configuration.
Auto-detects shell from
.B $SHELL
if not specified.
Use
.B init \-\-hook
to output shell code for manual integration.
Supported shells: bash, zsh, fish.
.TP
.BI add " name command"
Create or update an alias.
.TP
.BI rm " name" \fR " [\fB\-f\fR]"
Remove an alias.
Prompts for confirmation unless
.B \-f
is specified.
.TP
.BI ls " " \fR[\fIpattern\fR]
List all aliases, or filter by pattern.
.TP
.BI reload " " \fR[\fIshell\fR]
Output command to reload aliases.
Use with
.BR "eval \(dq$(am reload)\(dq" .
.TP
.B path
Show alias file path.
.TP
.B help
Show help message.
.TP
.B version
Show version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Force removal without confirmation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/am/aliases.txt
Default alias storage location.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/am/aliases.txt
Used if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AM_ALIAS_FILE
Override alias file location.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
XDG base directory for configuration files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Setup (run once):
.IP
.EX
am init
source ~/.bashrc
.EE
.PP
Add and use an alias:
.IP
.EX
am add gc "git commit -m"
eval "$(am reload)"
gc "initial commit"
.EE
.PP
List and filter aliases:
.IP
.EX
am ls
am ls git
.EE
.PP
Remove an alias:
.IP
.EX
am rm gc
am rm gc -f
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments
.TP
.B 2
File access error
.TP
.B 3
Home directory not found
.TP
.B 4
System error
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR alias (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1)
